  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="ES">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="ES">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="ES">1.) Existence of Cabinet endorsed Medium term strategy for strengthening of MSME Ecosystem. 
2.) Number of digital solutions adopted to address the COVID-19 pandemic 
-E-governance systems 
-Digital health systems 
-Data collection systems 
-Digital payment platforms 
-Digital e-commerce systems 
-Learning platforms 
Other 
3.) Number of private sector companies and formal and informal sector workers supported during and after the COVID-19 pandemic  
a) Micro, small, medium enterprises (MSMEs) ***data disagreggated to reflect Male, female and youth ownership 
b) Private sector companies, excluding MSMEs  
c) Formal sector workers  

d) Informal sector workers</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="ES">0</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="ES">1.) MSME Strategy to be completed and roll out. 
2.) Launch of VKC.
3.) Launch of Telecenters
4.) MSME Roadshows
5.) Carry out Intro to Digitization and Social Media Marketing and Content Creation to over 200 MSMEs</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="ES">1.) MSME strategy approved by Cabinet and nationally launched by the Prime Minister. 
2.) Completion of VKC with upload of digital trainings for access by public countrywide.
3.) Launch of 6 Telecenters with access to 30 workstations in rural and urban locations for MSME to access digital platforms to promote their businesses. 
4.) MSME roadshows were carried out in 9 different locations across the country. 
5.) Over 200 MSME including 70% women and 20% youth were trained in Intro to Digitization and Social Media Marketing and Content Creation .</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="ES">1.) SEIA on MSME results inform Medium term Strategy for strengthening of MSME Ecosystem finalized. 
2.) Digital/ virtual platform commissioned for use in MSME capacity building and knowledge exchange. Design and launch of a virtual knowledge center that supports e-learning, information sharing and B2B e-commerce. 
3.) Increase use of virtual knowledge center in MSME capacity development to be accessed and used by atleast 150 MSMEs whereby 60% is women and youth led. National communication campaign to increase the visibility of the VKC.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="ES">1.) SEIA was completed with over 350 businesses and a new MSME strategy is under development.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
